 a look at that island.

1752
00:59:33,740 --> 00:59:35,710
-All right, all right, we'll
 go to your damn, dirty island.

1753
00:59:35,710 --> 00:59:36,940
-I seem to remember
 some instructions

1754
00:59:36,940 --> 00:59:38,970
about not separating.

1755
00:59:38,970 --> 00:59:41,090
-We haven't run into anything
 we can't handle, Ralph.

1756
00:59:41,090 --> 00:59:43,540
-You know, I think they all
 read too much science fiction.

1757
00:59:43,540 --> 00:59:44,740
You know, they
 probably thought we'd

1758
00:59:44,740 --> 00:59:46,890
meet some kind of super
 race up here or something.

1759
00:59:46,890 --> 00:59:48,940
-And all we've met are
 large, mutated animals.

1760
00:59:48,940 --> 00:59:50,560
-Why don't we all go together?

1761
00:59:50,560 --> 00:59:51,630
-That bee was pretty super-race.

1762
00:59:51,630 --> 00:59:54,010
-Doctor, you know better
 than the rest of us

1763
00:59:54,010 --> 00:59:55,900
that you're in no
 shape to travel.

1764
00:59:55,900 --> 00:59:56,590
-That's right.

1765
00:59:56,590 --> 00:59:57,090
-Where is he?

1766
00:59:57,090 --> 00:59:59,220
-So Nora and I will take one
 of the rubber rafts tomorrow

1767
00:59:59,220 --> 01:00:00,930
and spend the day on the island.

1768
01:00:00,930 --> 01:00:04,310
Pat, you-- you do whatever
 work you can around here.

1769
01:00:04,310 --> 01:00:06,110
-Yeah, why don't you stay
 here and practice screaming.

1770
01:00:06,110 --> 01:00:07,080
[ROARING]

1771
01:00:07,080 --> 01:00:08,620
-Good, but back of the throat.

1772
01:00:08,620 --> 01:00:09,300
A little higher.

1773
01:00:11,890 --> 01:00:12,940
-Hi, remember me?

1774
01:00:12,940 --> 01:00:13,590
I'm Satan.

1775
01:00:13,590 --> 01:00:15,020
You never know where
 I'm going to pop up.

1776
01:00:15,020 --> 01:00:17,000
But first, a recipe
 from my pal, Ed Herlihy.

1777
01:00:19,890 --> 01:00:20,540
-[INAUDIBLE].

1778
01:00:20,540 --> 01:00:22,570
-What are we going to do
