-Sorry, that's a
 lizard from Pet World.

2342
01:21:21,670 --> 01:21:25,470
--just as similar ones dominated
 Earth 125 million years ago.

2343
01:21:25,470 --> 01:21:26,800
It's like living in the past.

2344
01:21:26,800 --> 01:21:28,370
-It's an iguana.

2345
01:21:28,370 --> 01:21:28,870
-Come on.

2346
01:21:28,870 --> 01:21:31,740
-Good likeness, isn't it?

2347
01:21:31,740 --> 01:21:33,170
-Well, who cares?

2348
01:21:33,170 --> 01:21:35,700
No one's ever going to believe
 us anyway, if we ever--

2349
01:21:35,700 --> 01:21:37,180
[LAUGHTER]

2350
01:21:37,180 --> 01:21:38,850
-That's a scientist for you.

2351
01:21:38,850 --> 01:21:39,710
-Hey, help me.

2352
01:21:39,710 --> 01:21:42,530
I don't like it when you fight.

2353
01:21:42,530 --> 01:21:44,060
-Meanwhile, three days later.

2354
01:21:44,060 --> 01:21:47,220
-And anyway, there's some
 real big jacks on this lake,

2355
01:21:47,220 --> 01:21:49,970
and I'm sure that
 if we just get some

2356
01:21:49,970 --> 01:21:51,650
time to drown a few slugs--

2357
01:21:51,650 --> 01:21:52,240
-Hey, look.

2358
01:21:52,240 --> 01:21:53,160
Lemur scat.

2359
01:21:53,160 --> 01:21:55,560
We must be getting close.

2360
01:21:55,560 --> 01:21:56,840
-Looks like Bob's.

2361
01:21:56,840 --> 01:21:59,710
-Listen to this music.

2362
01:21:59,710 --> 01:22:01,920
-What of Paul's love for Lena?

2363
01:22:01,920 --> 01:22:03,990
Will the lizards find
 peace in the valley?

2364
01:22:03,990 --> 01:22:07,330
And what of little
 Joey, the lemur?

2365
01:22:07,330 --> 01:22:08,670
You'll find out this and more--

2366
01:22:12,420 --> 01:22:14,800
-What's he gonna do,
 gull him to death?

2367
01:22:14,800 --> 01:22:17,500
-Ah, let me in there.

2368
01:22:17,500 --> 01:22:18,700
-If you come out
 of the woods today,

2369
01:22:18,700 --> 01:22:20,320
you're in for a big surprise.

2370
01:22:20,320 --> 01:22:21,860
If you're-- come
 on, keep up with me.

2371
01:22:21,860 --> 01:22:23,960
You go into the woods today,
 you won't believe your eyes.

2372
01:22:23,960 --> 01:22:24,460
[HUMMING].

2373
01:22:28,100 --> 01:22:30,210
Teddy bears having a picnic.

2374
01:22:30,210 --> 01:22:32,630
-You know, they're
 gonna be there tomorrow

2375
01:22:32,630 --> 01:22:33,960
afternoon at this pace.

2376
01:22:33,960 --> 01:22:35,500
-La, la, la.

2377
01:22:35,500 --> 01:22:37,460
-La, la, la.

2378
01:22:37,460 --> 01:22:39,550
-Who's this guy?

2379
01:22:39,550 --> 01:22:40,460
I don't know.

2380
01:22:40,460 --> 01:22:42,310
-And that's the day the teddy
 bears have their picnic.

2381
01:22:45,880 --> 01:22:46,460
-Take my hand.

2382
01:22:46,460 --> 01:22:48,860
I'm a stranger with parasites.

2383
01:22:48,860 --> 01:22:52,150
-Why do you have to bring
 your shoes everywhere?

2384
01:22:52,150 --> 01:22:53,130
-Give me that photo.

2385
01:22:53,130 --> 01:22:54,380
It's not a good likeness.

2386
01:22:54,380 --> 01:22:56,000
It looks like my passport photo.

2387
01:23:01,490 --> 01:23:01,990
-Mm.

2388
01:23:05,480 --> 01:23:08,430
-That's the day the
 teddy bears-- huh?

2389
01:23:08,430 --> 01:23:08,970
-We're closer.

2390
01:23:08,970 --> 01:23:10,310
-Yeah, the thing's lighter.

2391
01:23:10,310 --> 01:23:11,210
-In that canyon.

2392
01:23:11,210 --> 01:23:12,960
-Snack canyon.

2393
01:23:12,960 --> 01:23:14,160
-If you go out into
 the woods today,

2394
01:23:14,160 --> 01:23:15,210
you're in for a big surprise.

2395
01:23:15,210 --> 01:23:15,910
-Oh come on, shut up.

2396
01:23:15,910 --> 01:23:16,820
I need that song.

2397
01:23:16,820 --> 01:23:18,470
-Well, you're the one
 who started singing it.

2398
01:23:18,470 --> 01:23:19,030
-No, I didn't.

2399
01:23:19,030 --> 01:23:19,670
-Yes, you did.

2400
01:23:19,670 --> 01:23:20,470
-Hey, come on, you guys.

2401
01:23:20,470 --> 01:23:21,410
Stop fighting.

2402
01:23:21,410 --> 01:23:21,910
-Sorry.

2403
01:23:21,910 --> 01:23:23,840
I was doing a callback.

2404
01:23:23,840 --> 01:23:25,610
[CHUCKLING]

2405
01:23:25,610 --> 01:23:26,110
-Nyah, nyah.

2406
01:23:28,990 --> 01:23:29,490
-Sorry.

2407
01:23:33,260 --> 01:23:34,150
-Huh?
 -What?

2408
01:23:34,150 --> 01:23:34,770
What's going-- oh.

2409
01:23:37,940 --> 01:23:39,160
-Oh Ralph, what is it?

2410
01:23:39,160 --> 01:23:39,820
-It's an iguana.

2411
01:23:39,820 --> 01:23:40,470
Now, shut up.

2412
01:23:40,470 --> 01:23:41,600
-I don't know.

2413
01:23:41,600 --> 01:23:42,610
Something prehistoric.

2414
01:23:42,610 --> 01:23:43,760
-Oh, it's horrible.

2415
01:23:43,760 --> 01:23:46,080
-Oh, why do you have
 to be so negative.

2416
01:23:46,080 --> 01:23:46,990
-Shoot it with something.

2417
01:23:46,990 --> 01:23:47,570
-What with?

2418
01:23:47,570 --> 01:23:50,360
That won't do any good.

2419
01:23:50,360 --> 01:23:52,950
-Whoa.

2420
01:23:52,950 --> 01:23:54,350
[YAWNING]

2421
01:23:57,730 --> 01:23:58,580
-Hey, let go of my tail.

2422
01:23:58,580 --> 01:24:01,020
I want to get down there
 and mix it up a bit.

2423
01:24:01,020 --> 01:24:02,480
-Well, do something.

2424
01:24:02,480 --> 01:24:02,980
-Anything.

2425
01:24:02,980 --> 01:24:04,250
-We've got to get to them.

2426
01:24:04,250 --> 01:24:06,950
-No, they've got to get to us.

2427
01:24:06,950 --> 01:24:07,650
-OK, Joel.

2428
01:24:07,650 --> 01:24:09,120
I got $5 on the lizard.

2429
01:24:09,120 --> 01:24:10,030
-Get your money out.

2430
01:24:10,030 --> 01:24:11,170
-OK, I'll take your money.

2431
01:24:11,170 --> 01:24:11,960
OK, no problem.

2432
01:24:11,960 --> 01:24:13,530
Hey Crow, you're
 witness to that, OK?

2433
01:24:13,530 --> 01:24:14,560
-Hey, I want in on this action.

2434
01:24:14,560 --> 01:24:15,060
-OK.

2435
01:24:15,060 --> 01:24:17,370
-I'll bet 10 that they're are
 killed at the end of the film.

2436
01:24:17,370 --> 01:24:18,430
-OK.
 I'm holding the money.

2437
01:24:18,430 --> 01:24:19,040
-Wait a minute.

2438
01:24:19,040 --> 01:24:20,140
Wait a minute.
 What about our bet?

2439
01:24:20,140 --> 01:24:21,330
That's not fair.
 -Hey, you don't understand.

2440
01:24:21,330 --> 01:24:23,660
I'm playing the part of
 the expensive middleman.

2441
01:24:23,660 --> 01:24:25,160
This way, we all win.

2442
01:24:25,160 --> 01:24:25,850
-Oh.

2443
01:24:25,850 --> 01:24:26,350
-Huh?

2444
01:24:35,280 --> 01:24:38,260
-Buddy, if you pick at
 it, it'll never heal.

2445
01:24:38,260 --> 01:24:40,530
Whoa.

2446
01:24:40,530 --> 01:24:41,900
-Oh.

2447
01:24:41,900 --> 01:24:43,280
-Ooh, Jesus.

2448
01:24:43,280 --> 01:24:43,980
-Ah, come on, lizard.

2449
01:24:43,980 --> 01:24:44,480
Come on.

2450
01:24:44,480 --> 01:24:45,630
Daddy needs a new pair of shoes.

2451
01:24:45,630 --> 01:24:47,140
Come on, i got money on this.

2452
01:24:47,140 --> 01:24:49,240
-Luck, be a lizard tonight.

2453
01:24:49,240 --> 01:24:51,490
Come on.

2454
01:24:51,490 --> 01:24:51,990
-Help.

2455
01:24:51,990 --> 01:24:53,410
I'm hooked in your braces.

2456
01:24:53,410 --> 01:24:56,010
[MUFFLED]

2457
01:24:56,010 --> 01:25:00,250
-I saw this on
 "Midnight Express" once.

2458
01:25:00,250 --> 01:25:00,750
-Ouch.

2459
01:25:03,330 --> 01:25:07,210
-Oh, that'd be a lot
 more fun on a toboggan.

2460
01:25:07,210 --> 01:25:08,980
-That sounds like
 lizards dropping.

2461
01:25:11,610 --> 01:25:13,720
-Sorry I tore your picture.

2462
01:25:13,720 --> 01:25:15,270
-Sorry I ripped your dress.

2463
01:25:15,270 --> 01:25:17,390
-Sorry I smashed your lunchbox.

2464
01:25:17,390 --> 01:25:18,950
-Sorry I broke your heart.

2465
01:25:21,770 --> 01:25:25,820
-Giant mutated lizards-- wish
 we had some pictures of it.

2466
01:25:25,820 --> 01:25:27,990
-Doh!

2467
01:25:27,990 --> 01:25:30,040
-They're running through
 dino-scat over there.

2468
01:25:30,040 --> 01:25:30,890
-Faster.

2469
01:25:30,890 --> 01:25:31,540
-Up yours.

2470
01:25:31,540 --> 01:25:33,520
I mean, we'll be right there.

2471
01:25:36,700 --> 01:25:38,770
[GROANING]

2472
01:25:38,770 --> 01:25:41,320
-I don't care if you are a
 lizard, that has to hurt.

2473
01:25:41,320 --> 01:25:42,280
-Oh, man.

2474
01:25:42,280 --> 01:25:44,210
That's got to really sting.

2475
01:25:47,020 --> 01:25:49,900
-Get up there, you
 stupid culotted little--

2476
01:25:49,900 --> 01:25:50,400
-Oh, Ralph.

2477
01:25:50,400 --> 01:25:51,340
Will they make it?

2478
01:25:51,340 --> 01:25:52,820
-Sure, they're going to make it.

2479
01:25:52,820 --> 01:25:53,960
-Or they're going to die trying.

2480
01:25:53,960 --> 01:25:54,460
-Come on.

2481
01:25:57,300 --> 01:26:00,870
-Come on, you buttheads.

2482
01:26:00,870 --> 01:26:03,110
-You know, guys,
 lizards were hurt

2483
01:26:03,110 --> 01:26:04,930
in the making of this film.

2484
01:26:04,930 --> 01:26:07,400
-Ah!

2485
01:26:07,400 --> 01:26:08,590
-That's almost a reversal.

2486
01:26:08,590 --> 01:26:10,750
That would have been two points.

2487
01:26:10,750 --> 01:26:12,920
-Oh, I'm filled with shame.

2488
01:26:12,920 --> 01:26:14,930
Oh, Rob.

2489
01:26:14,930 --> 01:26:20,390
-All right, now that that's
 done, where's Lipper.t

2490
01:26:20,390 --> 01:26:22,110
I'm coming for you.

2491
01:26:22,110 --> 01:26:23,610
Payback time.

2492
01:26:23,610 --> 01:26:24,890
-Yeah.

2493
01:26:24,890 --> 01:26:28,750
-Looks like a
 Cajun cooking show.

2494
01:26:28,750 --> 01:26:29,520
-Oh, honey.

2495
01:26:29,520 --> 01:26:30,430
-I brought the atom bomb.

2496
01:26:30,430 --> 01:26:31,660
I think it's a good
 time to use it.

2497
01:26:31,660 --> 01:26:34,400
-Oh, that's your
 answer to everything.

2498
01:26:34,400 --> 01:26:36,150
just use the atom bomb.

2499
01:26:36,150 --> 01:26:39,550
-Hey, what's going
 on, peace friends?

2500
01:26:39,550 --> 01:26:40,390
-It's set for 8 o'clock.

2501
01:26:40,390 --> 01:26:42,820
-And right now, it's
 30 seconds to 8:00.

2502
01:26:42,820 --> 01:26:44,200
-Whoa!

2503
01:26:44,200 --> 01:26:46,490
-Oh, it's a joke.

2504
01:26:46,490 --> 01:26:48,650
-(LAUGHING) I win.

2505
01:26:48,650 --> 01:26:49,890
Ha, ha, ha!

2506
01:26:49,890 --> 01:26:52,090
And I know where you live.

2507
01:26:52,090 --> 01:26:55,750
-Whoa-ho, wrong turn, friends.

2508
01:26:55,750 --> 01:26:57,500
-Ah, big and-- ah, yes.

2509
01:26:57,500 --> 01:26:58,600
-Hey, what did he ever do?

2510
01:26:58,600 --> 01:26:59,720
-He was on the
 cover of "Tarkus."

2511
01:26:59,720 --> 01:27:00,220
-Oh, OK.

2512
01:27:00,220 --> 01:27:02,790
Shoot him.

2513
01:27:02,790 --> 01:27:04,450
[IMITATING SOUNDTRACK]

2514
01:27:04,450 --> 01:27:07,220
-Na, na, na-- this music
 sounds like it was written

2515
01:27:07,220 --> 01:27:09,060
by Lori Strong,
 you know the girl

2516
01:27:09,060 --> 01:27:11,050
who teased me in third grade.

2517
01:27:11,050 --> 01:27:13,700
-Even the musicians
 are mocking this film.

2518
01:27:13,700 --> 01:27:16,110
-Nyah, nyah, nyah--

2519
01:27:16,110 --> 01:27:19,570
-Oh, it sounded
 like an airplane.

2520
01:27:19,570 --> 01:27:20,900
-Oh, I just want to be friends.

2521
01:27:20,900 --> 01:27:22,150
Please come back.

2522
01:27:22,150 --> 01:27:24,680
My friends.

2523
01:27:24,680 --> 01:27:27,800
-You know, sometimes
 my own species

2524
01:27:27,800 --> 01:27:30,920
makes me feel ashamed, what
 they're doing to this dinosaur.

2525
01:27:30,920 --> 01:27:31,980
-Come on, let's go.

2526
01:27:31,980 --> 01:27:32,480
-Whoa.

2527
01:27:36,870 --> 01:27:38,100
-I'm your new boyfriend now.

2528
01:27:38,100 --> 01:27:39,960
Ha, ha.

2529
01:27:39,960 --> 01:27:41,350
-Everybody panic.

2530
01:27:41,350 --> 01:27:42,740
[SCREAMING]

2531
01:27:42,740 --> 01:27:46,210
-When in danger or in doubt, run
 in circles, scream and shout.

2532
01:27:46,210 --> 01:27:47,620
Whoa!

2533
01:27:47,620 --> 01:27:49,500
Help me.

2534
01:27:49,500 --> 01:27:51,400
-There they go.

2535
01:27:51,400 --> 01:27:53,520
-Calm and reassured.

2536
01:27:53,520 --> 01:27:55,940
-Nyah, nyah, nyah--

2537
01:27:55,940 --> 01:27:57,510
-Oh, welcome to Pamplona.

2538
01:27:57,510 --> 01:27:59,120
-This week on
 "Living Dangerously,"

2539
01:27:59,120 --> 01:28:00,800
hand-delivered atomic bombs.

2540
01:28:00,800 --> 01:28:02,890
-Green alligators,
 long-necked geese, and--

2541
01:28:02,890 --> 01:28:05,860
-Monkey-back camel, and I
 saw chimpanzees up there.

2542
01:28:05,860 --> 01:28:10,610
-I'm coming, beaty boy, ooh-hoo.

2543
01:28:10,610 --> 01:28:11,270
-Wow.

2544
01:28:11,270 --> 01:28:12,940
-Get a load of this.

2545
01:28:12,940 --> 01:28:14,510
How did they get him
 to shake like that?

2546
01:28:14,510 --> 01:28:17,150
-They covered him
 with shag carpeting.

2547
01:28:17,150 --> 01:28:19,350
-Poor elephant.

2548
01:28:19,350 --> 01:28:22,090
-I'm not an animal.

2549
01:28:22,090 --> 01:28:23,740
-It's a good shot.

2550
01:28:23,740 --> 01:28:24,930
[SHOUT]

2551
01:28:24,930 --> 01:28:26,060
-If you go out in
 the woods today,

2552
01:28:26,060 --> 01:28:27,320
you're in for a big surprise.

2553
01:28:27,320 --> 01:28:28,180
Heh.

2554
01:28:28,180 --> 01:28:29,590
-Save yourselves, man.

2555
01:28:29,590 --> 01:28:31,340
There's a bomb back there.

2556
01:28:34,180 --> 01:28:34,820
-Nyah, nyah, nyah--

2557
01:28:37,800 --> 01:28:40,790
-Ugh.

2558
01:28:40,790 --> 01:28:44,910
-This is an exciting run.

2559
01:28:44,910 --> 01:28:45,480
-Whoa.

2560
01:28:45,480 --> 01:28:47,320
-Hey, it's the MGM lion.

2561
01:28:47,320 --> 01:28:50,670
-No, it's the Lippert lizard.

2562
01:28:50,670 --> 01:28:52,230
-OK, you beat me.

2563
01:28:52,230 --> 01:28:53,950
Get out of here, you bums.

2564
01:28:53,950 --> 01:28:54,820
Take--

2565
01:28:54,820 --> 01:28:58,040
-Why can't they stop
 hurting each other?

2566
01:28:58,040 --> 01:28:59,340
Come on, man.

2567
01:29:02,110 --> 01:29:04,840
[IMITATING SOUNDTRACK]

2568
01:29:04,840 --> 01:29:05,440
-Jeepers, friends.

2569
01:29:05,440 --> 01:29:06,210
Wait for me.

2570
01:29:06,210 --> 01:29:08,140
-I was wondering about him.

2571
01:29:08,140 --> 01:29:09,810
-To the beach!

2572
01:29:09,810 --> 01:29:11,690
Kind of like Dunkirk,
 isn't it, guys?

2573
01:29:15,970 --> 01:29:17,060
-I'm just a poor turtle.

2574
01:29:17,060 --> 01:29:18,480
Help, Mr. Wizard.

2575
01:29:18,480 --> 01:29:20,960
Help.

2576
01:29:20,960 --> 01:29:21,950
-Hey!

2577
01:29:21,950 --> 01:29:22,950
-Hey!

2578
01:29:22,950 --> 01:29:24,930
-Hey!

2579
01:29:24,930 --> 01:29:26,360
-They're leaving
 the other boats.

2580
01:29:26,360 --> 01:29:28,520
-Uh, I think that's
 for the lemur.

2581
01:29:28,520 --> 01:29:31,160
-Oh.

2582
01:29:31,160 --> 01:29:36,790
-Stroke, stroke, stroke, stroke.

2583
01:29:36,790 --> 01:29:37,710
-Hey, get me.

2584
01:29:37,710 --> 01:29:38,790
I'm a Hasidic rabbi.

2585
01:29:38,790 --> 01:29:39,290
Shalom.

2586
01:29:42,840 --> 01:29:46,780
-Kind of like you're
 on "Hawaii 5-0!"

2587
01:29:46,780 --> 01:29:48,130
-Ah, phooey.

2588
01:29:48,130 --> 01:29:49,560
No one got the joke.

2589
01:29:52,590 --> 01:29:55,010
-I think he's just scooping
 water into the boat there.

2590
01:29:57,920 --> 01:29:58,420
-Hm.

2591
01:30:01,750 --> 01:30:02,870
-Hey, anybody have the time?

2592
01:30:02,870 --> 01:30:05,110
There's a little matter
 of an atomic bomb.

2593
01:30:05,110 --> 01:30:05,790
-Oh, yeah.

2594
01:30:05,790 --> 01:30:09,000
-(SINGING) Your careers
 are finally almost over.

2595
01:30:09,000 --> 01:30:11,860
You'll never be in another film.

2596
01:30:11,860 --> 01:30:14,710
You may end up in the
 "Psychotronic Film Guide."

2597
01:30:14,710 --> 01:30:16,840
-Huh?

2598
01:30:16,840 --> 01:30:19,200
-Hey, isn't that
 where Bob upchucked?

2599
01:30:19,200 --> 01:30:21,310
It looks like the
 Valdez has been here.

2600
01:30:21,310 --> 01:30:26,150
And there's something-- I can
 taste carrots in the water.

2601
01:30:26,150 --> 01:30:28,050
[IMITATING SOUNDTRACK]

2602
01:30:31,260 --> 01:30:32,660
-Huh?

2603
01:30:32,660 --> 01:30:35,470
Uh-oh.

2604
01:30:35,470 --> 01:30:37,280
You know, I think
 the film on this lake

2605
01:30:37,280 --> 01:30:38,660
is better than the
 film we're watching.

2606
01:30:42,080 --> 01:30:44,400
-Look, he's pushing her
 down again for no reason.

2607
01:30:44,400 --> 01:30:45,860
Look at him.

2608
01:30:45,860 --> 01:30:49,260
That's terrible.

2609
01:30:49,260 --> 01:30:50,610
-Just tear out of there.

2610
01:30:50,610 --> 01:30:52,010
-Let's go.

2611
01:30:52,010 --> 01:30:52,700
-Hurry up.

2612
01:30:52,700 --> 01:30:53,400
-Cheese it, everyone.

2613
01:30:53,400 --> 01:30:54,800
-Don't forget me.

2614
01:30:54,800 --> 01:30:55,730
Please.

2615
01:30:55,730 --> 01:30:58,870
-Oh, they tripped
 over a burial mound.

2616
01:30:58,870 --> 01:30:59,700
How fitting.

2617
01:30:59,700 --> 01:31:02,910
-You should just
 pull her by her hair.

2618
01:31:02,910 --> 01:31:03,410
-Oops.

2619
01:31:03,410 --> 01:31:05,870
-Damn.

2620
01:31:05,870 --> 01:31:08,230
-Ahh!

2621
01:31:08,230 --> 01:31:09,950
-That's the biggest
 firework of all.

2622
01:31:09,950 --> 01:31:13,110
-Looks like the beginning
 of "Petticoat Junction."

2623
01:31:13,110 --> 01:31:15,340
Petticoat Armageddon.

2624
01:31:15,340 --> 01:31:17,900
-Shouldn't they be covering
 their faces or something?

2625
01:31:17,900 --> 01:31:19,420
Or shields or--

2626
01:31:19,420 --> 01:31:21,720
-Uh, why?

2627
01:31:21,720 --> 01:31:22,350
-I don't know.

2628
01:31:22,350 --> 01:31:23,400
It just--

2629
01:31:23,400 --> 01:31:24,750
-Nuclear blast fallout?

2630
01:31:24,750 --> 01:31:26,290
-Yeah.

2631
01:31:26,290 --> 01:31:28,790
-Uh, we did the right
 thing, didn't we?

2632
01:31:28,790 --> 01:31:30,630
They'd never surrender.

2633
01:31:30,630 --> 01:31:31,970
It was right for
 us to blow them up.

2634
01:31:31,970 --> 01:31:34,120
-Thanks for annihilating
 everything I know.

2635
01:31:37,430 --> 01:31:39,400
-You know, they're only
 two miles from the blast.

2636
01:31:39,400 --> 01:31:40,810
Aren't they going
 to get vaporized?

2637
01:31:40,810 --> 01:31:42,560
-I hope so.

2638
01:31:42,560 --> 01:31:44,190
Well, it's an atom
 bomb light, actually.

2639
01:31:44,190 --> 01:31:46,100
1/3 as destructive
 as our other bomb.

2640
01:31:46,100 --> 01:31:46,600
-Oh.

2641
01:31:49,670 --> 01:31:52,800
-Well, score one for Earth.

2642
01:31:52,800 --> 01:31:55,850
-Well, we've done it.

2643
01:31:55,850 --> 01:31:59,200
-Not a word of this gets out to
 the people on Earth, all right?

2644
01:31:59,200 --> 01:32:00,990
-We sure have done it.

2645
01:32:00,990 --> 01:32:05,190
We brought civilization
 to Planet Nova.

2646
01:32:05,190 --> 01:32:06,590
-Ha, was that irony?

2647
01:32:06,590 --> 01:32:07,200
-Come on.

2648
01:32:07,200 --> 01:32:07,970
-This late in the film?

2649
01:32:07,970 --> 01:32:10,320
-Let's go home.

2650
01:32:10,320 --> 01:32:13,730
-Yeah, let's go home and
 grow some three-headed kids.

2651
01:32:13,730 --> 01:32:16,430
-Hey, there's a certain
 glow about June.

2652
01:32:16,430 --> 01:32:20,630
Heh-- it's a-- never mind.

2653
01:32:20,630 --> 01:32:22,780
-And so with peace
 in their hearts

2654
01:32:22,780 --> 01:32:25,400
and fiery death in the
 sky, they went home.

2655
01:32:30,020 --> 01:32:31,800
-Kinda pretty in an ugly way.

2656
01:32:31,800 --> 01:32:33,430
-I like it.

2657
01:32:33,430 --> 01:32:33,930
Bah.

2658
01:32:59,450 --> 01:33:00,440
-Hey--

2659
01:33:00,440 --> 01:33:02,910
-You guys, that's the
 fourth Robert Lippert

2660
01:33:02,910 --> 01:33:05,070
film we've seen
 in as many months.

2661
01:33:05,070 --> 01:33:08,410
Remember "Rocketship
 XM," "Jungle Goddess,"

2662
01:33:08,410 --> 01:33:12,100
"Lost Continent," and now
 this one, "King Dinosaur."

2663
01:33:12,100 --> 01:33:14,990
I've never even seen
 a Kurosawa film.

2664
01:33:14,990 --> 01:33:16,240
Works of Francois Truffaut?

2665
01:33:16,240 --> 01:33:16,740
Uh-uh.

2666
01:33:16,740 --> 01:33:17,590
Not familiar with them.

2667
01:33:17,590 --> 01:33:18,160
Sorry.

2668
01:33:18,160 --> 01:33:19,400
Odessa steps sequence?

2669
01:33:19,400 --> 01:33:20,790
I don't think I know that one.

2670
01:33:20,790 --> 01:33:21,290
No.

2671
01:33:21,290 --> 01:33:24,940
And yet I'm intimately familiar,
 with a frame-by-frame basis,

2672
01:33:24,940 --> 01:33:27,660
with a major part of one
 Robert L. Lippert's output.

2673
01:33:27,660 --> 01:33:28,610
Why?

2674
01:33:28,610 --> 01:33:29,420
Why?
 Why?

2675
01:33:29,420 --> 01:33:30,150
I don't understand it.

2676
01:33:30,150 --> 01:33:30,650
I--

2677
01:33:30,650 --> 01:33:31,250
-Crow.

2678
01:33:31,250 --> 01:33:31,750
Crow.

2679
01:33:31,750 --> 01:33:33,450
Hey, take it easy.

2680
01:33:33,450 --> 01:33:34,120
There's no need to--

2681
01:33:34,120 --> 01:33:34,950
-Hey, Crow's right, Joel.

2682
01:33:34,950 --> 01:33:38,350
You know, there's only so
 much that we can take, really.

2683
01:33:38,350 --> 01:33:40,180
-Well, the fact
 is, you guys might

2684
01:33:40,180 --> 01:33:43,110
be surprised to know that Robert
 Lippert was quite an innovator

2685
01:33:43,110 --> 01:33:44,040
in his time.

2686
01:33:44,040 --> 01:33:44,980
-Oh, really?

2687
01:33:44,980 --> 01:33:46,980
-In fact, I've prepared a
 special presentation using

2688
01:33:46,980 --> 01:33:47,480
our--

2689
01:33:47,480 --> 01:33:48,550
-No, no, no, no.

2690
01:33:48,550 --> 01:33:49,050
No you don't.

2691
01:33:49,050 --> 01:33:51,470
-No, no, no, no, no, no.

2692
01:33:51,470 --> 01:33:52,640
-Oh, You don't want to see that?

2693
01:33:52,640 --> 01:33:55,110
Well, fortunately Cambot
 and I have worked up

2694
01:33:55,110 --> 01:33:57,050
a little sound and light show.

2695
01:33:57,050 --> 01:33:58,760
Cambot, cue that up, please.

2696
01:33:58,760 --> 01:33:59,590
-No.

2697
01:33:59,590 --> 01:34:00,590
Stop the music.

2698
01:34:00,590 --> 01:34:03,580
Cue that light, Cambot,
 or I'll kill you.

2699
01:34:03,580 --> 01:34:05,450
-That's better.

2700
01:34:05,450 --> 01:34:07,440
-Well, I don't see
 why it would bug you

2701
01:34:07,440 --> 01:34:08,690
that I would try
 to do such a thing.

2702
01:34:08,690 --> 01:34:11,310
-Because those artist's
 renderings, musical tributes,

2703
01:34:11,310 --> 01:34:12,100
I don't think so, Joel.

2704
01:34:12,100 --> 01:34:13,030
Come on.

2705
01:34:13,030 --> 01:34:14,690
-I'm just trying
 to show you that--

2706
01:34:14,690 --> 01:34:16,600
-Joel, Lippert is not worth it.

2707
01:34:16,600 --> 01:34:18,040
No, no.

2708
01:34:18,040 --> 01:34:20,270
-Well, there's just
 one thing that he

2709
01:34:20,270 --> 01:34:21,520
did that I would
 like to show you,

2710
01:34:21,520 --> 01:34:23,610
because I spent a lot of time
 in the shop working on it.

2711
01:34:23,610 --> 01:34:24,610
Here it is.

2712
01:34:24,610 --> 01:34:25,790
-Show us your little toy.

2713
01:34:25,790 --> 01:34:27,450
-Robert Lippert was
 the first filmmaker

2714
01:34:27,450 --> 01:34:29,650
to ever use a thing
 called a theremin.

2715
01:34:29,650 --> 01:34:33,600
And a theremin creates
 a body of particles.

2716
01:34:33,600 --> 01:34:34,860
And when you interrupt
 the particles,

2717
01:34:34,860 --> 01:34:35,880
it changes the sound.

2718
01:34:35,880 --> 01:34:38,190
You may have heard it in
 other space movies before.

2719
01:34:38,190 --> 01:34:38,690
-Sure.

2720
01:34:38,690 --> 01:34:39,660
-Here, let's turn it on here.

2721
01:34:39,660 --> 01:34:40,430
Let's try it.

2722
01:34:40,430 --> 01:34:42,420
-Oh, that's rather
 pleasing, isn't it?

2723
01:34:42,420 --> 01:34:43,720
-Yeah.

2724
01:34:43,720 --> 01:34:44,400
-Neat.

2725
01:34:44,400 --> 01:34:45,250
-Whoa.

2726
01:34:45,250 --> 01:34:47,080
That's interesting
 the way it changes--

2727
01:34:47,080 --> 01:34:47,970
-Sounds like--

2728
01:34:47,970 --> 01:34:49,370
-Well, thank you
 very much for sharing

2729
01:34:49,370 --> 01:34:50,490
your little toy with us, Joel.

2730
01:34:50,490 --> 01:34:51,830
You can turn it
 off any time, now.

2731
01:34:51,830 --> 01:34:52,330
-Thank you.

2732
01:34:52,330 --> 01:34:53,260
-It starts to get a little--

2733
01:34:53,260 --> 01:34:54,910
-Thank you, Robert Klein.

2734
01:34:54,910 --> 01:34:55,720
Thank you.

2735
01:34:55,720 --> 01:34:56,430
-Thanks a lot.

2736
01:34:56,430 --> 01:34:59,420
OK, so why don't you take that
 down to your cabin, there Joel?

2737
01:35:01,940 --> 01:35:02,700
Joel?

2738
01:35:02,700 --> 01:35:04,910
I guess it's up to us to
 take care of business.

2739
01:35:04,910 --> 01:35:05,400
-Guess so.

2740
01:35:05,400 --> 01:35:06,040
[CRASHING]

2741
01:35:06,040 --> 01:35:08,500
-Oh, just set that
 anywhere, Joel.

2742
01:35:08,500 --> 01:35:09,450
Hope he didn't break it.

2743
01:35:09,450 --> 01:35:12,040
Well, so let's read this
 letter that's down here.

2744
01:35:12,040 --> 01:35:13,160
-Yep, go ahead.

2745
01:35:13,160 --> 01:35:15,560
-Uh, after he leaves.

2746
01:35:15,560 --> 01:35:19,050
Joel, could you please--
 so it says here--

2747
01:35:19,050 --> 01:35:19,940
[CRASHING]

2748
01:35:19,940 --> 01:35:21,170
-Joel, if it bends it's funny.

2749
01:35:21,170 --> 01:35:22,990
If it breaks, it's not funny.

2750
01:35:22,990 --> 01:35:23,680
-Yikes.

2751
01:35:23,680 --> 01:35:25,840
OK, it says, dear
 sirs, it's us again,

2752
01:35:25,840 --> 01:35:28,590
the Mistys from Milwaukee,
 with our weekly approbations

2753
01:35:28,590 --> 01:35:29,600
of doom.

2754
01:35:29,600 --> 01:35:32,390
As usual, we-- uh,
 thank you, Joel-- we

2755
01:35:32,390 --> 01:35:33,660
had a great time
 with the latest show.

2756
01:35:33,660 --> 01:35:35,630
We wanted to point out a
 few things regarding the--

2757
01:35:35,630 --> 01:35:36,480
[CRASHING]

2758
01:35:36,480 --> 01:35:37,600
-Thank you again, Joel.

2759
01:35:37,600 --> 01:35:39,750
Enclosed-- hey, they
 enclosed some scorecards.

2760
01:35:39,750 --> 01:35:40,580
Hey Cambot, put these up.

2761
01:35:40,580 --> 01:35:41,950
These are really interesting.

2762
01:35:41,950 --> 01:35:44,640
Now look, they actually rate
 us on a scale of 1 to 10

2763
01:35:44,640 --> 01:35:48,840
on the movie, on sarcasm,
 on the invention exchange,

2764
01:35:48,840 --> 01:35:50,130
and these host segments.

2765
01:35:50,130 --> 01:35:51,760
What are host segments?

2766
01:35:51,760 --> 01:35:52,870
-Uh, I don't know.

2767
01:35:52,870 --> 01:35:53,880
-Got me on that one.

2768
01:35:53,880 --> 01:35:55,210
OK, now what are we
 supposed to do now?

2769
01:35:55,210 --> 01:35:57,810
-Uh, say something
 to the scientists.

2770
01:35:57,810 --> 01:35:58,310
-Oh.

2771
01:35:58,310 --> 01:35:59,610
Hey guys, are you watching?

2772
01:35:59,610 --> 01:36:00,640
How did it go?

2773
01:36:00,640 --> 01:36:01,240
What do you think?

2774
01:36:01,240 --> 01:36:04,780
-I think we should go
 to the Kurosawa Festival

2775
01:36:04,780 --> 01:36:06,030
at the Geripera Cinema.

2776
01:36:06,030 --> 01:36:07,050
What do you think, Frank?

2777
01:36:07,050 --> 01:36:08,050
-Oh, forget that.

2778
01:36:08,050 --> 01:36:09,700
What about the theremin?

2779
01:36:09,700 --> 01:36:12,370
Woo--

2780
01:36:12,370 --> 01:36:13,980
-I have another idea.

2781
01:36:13,980 --> 01:36:15,860
Until next time, Joel-y.

2782
01:36:18,670 --> 01:36:19,170
-Rest.

2783
01:36:22,020 --> 01:37:32,300
[MUSIC PLAYING]

